   Providence, RI, JUL 21-25, 2024},
Abstract = {CMB-S4 is a large-scale scientific experiment jointly funded by NSF and
   DOE to measure with exquisite detail radiation emitted just after the
   Big Bang, accessing Physics at energy scales way above what is
   achievable with collider experiments. CMB-S4 data will need to be made
   available first internally to the Collaboration involving more than 500
   scientists and then to the wider Astrophysics scientific community. In
   this paper we present a prototype data repository that combines Globus
