Note = {IEEE International Conference on Industrial Cyber Physical Systems
   (ICPS), Taipei, TAIWAN, MAY 06-09, 2019},
Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; IEEE Ind Elect Soc},
Abstract = {Pervasive computing envisions environments where computers are blended
   into our environment to provide services. This vision is today very
   popular and a number of pervasive platforms are already used today in
   smart homes, buildings or plants. Many platforms today are based on
   service-oriented computing. This allows to deal with dynamicity and
   heterogeneity issues. However, this approach is not adapted to
   applications based on flows of time-stamped data. In this paper, we
   present a service-oriented platform extended with a time-series
   database. This platform can host a variety of applications with
   different requirements regarding data to be manipulated. This is
   demonstrated in the industry 4.0 domain and, more precisely, on a water
   management application.},
