   (ICCE-ASIA)},
Year = {2021},
Note = {IEEE International Conference on Consumer Electronics-Asia (ICCE-Asia),
   SOUTH KOREA, NOV 01-03, 2021},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {Improvements in genome technology have been substantially increasing the
   available amount of gene data. As the gene data contain sensitive
   personal information, security schemes that can ensure confidentiality
   and safe sharing are necessary. In this paper, we propose a model for
   secure gene data management using blockchain and encryption. The
   proposed model employs a storage where the gene data are partially
   encrypted, and access control for the data is ensured by the blockchain
   so that the data can be shared safely. Furthermore, the gene owner can
   trace the usage and status of the data using a decentralized
   application.},
