Pages = {382-391},
Note = {3rd International Conference on Digital Technologies and Applications,
   MOROCCO, JAN 27-28, 2023},
Abstract = {Education is one of the key sectors that suffered significantly in this
   pandemic. With 35 million students enrolled in its higher educational
   institutions, India has been grappling with various technological
   challenges, such as effective data management - the issue of generating,
   handling, and securing millions of Gigabytes of information. The
   Education Information System needs a technological overhaul to face
   unprecedented times. The paper delivers a brief understanding of Big
   data and blockchain technology, followed by an observation of the Indian
   higher educational sector, the challenges, and if Blockchain could be a
   veritable solution for addressing these challenges. The ramifications of
   such a change and the scope for future research on Information systems
   are deliberate. This theoretical study investigates the impact
   blockchain technology could have on the higher education sector. The
   slow adoption of blockchain technology in education mirrors some serious
   problems, such as the lack of concrete incentives for blockchain mining.
   This paradox of weighing Blockchain's benefits with the issues in
   adopting the technology is critically discussed.},
