Pages = {85-91},
Note = {9th International Conference on Big Data Analytics-ICBDA-Annual, Waseda
   University, Tokyo, JAPAN, MAR 16-18, 2024},
Organization = {Oslo Metropolitan University (OsloMet); National Institute of Technology
   and Evaluation; California State University East Bay},
Abstract = {This paper presents a dedicated data management platform designed for
   efficiently determining material process flow, complemented by a
   customized big data search system tailored for Material Informatics
   (MI). The material manufacturing sector heavily depends on intricate
   process flow for product development. Material industries increasingly
   adopt modern technology to optimize product quality, quantity, and
   resource conservation, and developing new materials is intricate,
   demanding a deep understanding of the process flow steps. Effective
   resource management remains challenging for the data management
   platform. Process flow assists the analytical approach to developing big
   data management, such as data similarity identification based on user
   requirements. Process flow can easily be represented in a graph, making
   it easy for analytical analysis. Graphical representations aid in
   control and innovation for big data management. Our novel approach
   utilizes an advanced graph similarity method incorporating Hamiltonian
   paths and sophisticated machine learning algorithms. We have
   incorporated a graph similarity procedure to pinpoint control steps. In
   product development, finding the principal flow graph is vital. Our data
   management platform aids R\&D in discovering efficient pathways,
   offering a swift response. Our method's path similarity scores matching
   yields 73\%, with 87\% topology similarity and 86\% node data matching.},
