Abstract = {Reproducibility is a significant challenge in (epi)genomic research due
   to the complexity of experiments composed of traditional biochemistry
   and informatics. Recent advances have exacerbated this as
   high-throughput sequencing data is generated at an unprecedented pace.
   Here, we report the development of a Platform for Epi-Genomic Research
   (PEGR), a web-based project management platform that tracks and quality
   controls experiments from conception to publication-ready figures,
   compatible with multiple assays and bioinformatic pipelines. It supports
   rigor and reproducibility for biochemists working at the bench, while
   fully supporting reproducibility and reliability for bioinformaticians
   through integration with the Galaxy platform.},
