   SEP 16-19, 2018},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {As the application of IoT systems becomes more and more widespread, the
   increasing complexity of modern hardware and software platform along
   with the imperative assurance on stability deems runtime verification of
   task fulfillment necessary in IoT ecosystems. Nevertheless, distributing
   the burden of a central verification monitor to individual devices could
   improve the efficiency. To achieve the decentralized runtime
   verification, this work investigates and incorporates some of the
   mechanisms of blockchain technology into IoT ecosystems for locating the
