Abstract = {Many industrials consider blockchain as a technology breakthrough for
   cybersecurity, with use cases ranging from cryptocurrency system to
   smart contracts, and so forth. While IoT systems employ a lightweight
   communication protocol between physical objects, blockchain may ensure
   safe information gathering. Unfortunately, the mixture of both
   technologies has yet to be formally investigated regarding the consensus
   algorithm. In this paper, statistical model checking is applied to
   provide quantitative answers on whether the modeled system satisfies
